  "notes": {
    "base": "New base: arm A is upstream dev 736a0682d38f0a1c6592f34b1c6749fea221da42 ('Merge pull request #2255 from JustVugg/perf/cuda-f32-gemm'), after PR #0 (#2212-#2217) merged; the final4 manifests (../final4) used dev 62eaa9dc249b67567b9cbc83e43fbc875a8b94c1. The pr1 tip 34fe3f808d348f28e0813b02f42eeea14c2414d3 (refresh/pr1-reap-prefill, tree 517adae7cb35c09eb59ee2588989d659a589bfa2) is 8 commits on top of this base (meta/tips.txt: dev_is_ancestor_of_pr1=yes). dev still refuses the batched GPU MoE for the 132-expert model: every A serve.log has 'v4_gpu moe-batch=off (unsupported model geometry)', every B/C serve.log 'v4_gpu moe-batch=on bank=132-experts', and only C 'v4_gpu moe-double=on'.",
    "prewarm": "Expert-cache prewarm: the base includes upstream #2111 (463f8443, 'a serve fills the expert cache before its first request (#2109)'), so both dev and the pr1 tip prewarm at serve start. At --ram 40 the plan holds 59 of 132 experts per layer, so the prewarm picks experts from .coli_usage, which was empty (size 0, same mtime) before and after every sample (sample.txt usage_before/usage_after; summary.json usage_history_changed []). Every A/B/C serve.log says '[v4] expert cache: 59 of 132 experts per layer fit and no usage history says which, so it fills as experts are used': the prewarm read nothing, and the expert cache started empty in every sample as on 2026-10-15.",
    "cache_state": "The OS page cache was not dropped between samples. The run began with one discarded warm-up sample W (seq 1, a separate server process on the pr1 tip, both requests; texts identical to the reference) before A s1. Unlike the 2026-10-15 run, no host journal was captured for this window, so the serve unit's memory peak (used then to show round 1 was partly cold) is not available and the cache state per sample cannot be stated from evidence. Observed: A request-1 TTFT s1 131.475 s vs s2/s3 130.159/129.009 s (s1 1.46% slower than the s2/s3 mean); medians are over all 3 samples. Run order (seq 2-10): A s1 B s1 C s1 B s2 C s2 A s2 C s3 A s3 B s3.",
    "variability": "TTFT stdev / CV over 3 samples, every arm and request: A r1 1.234 s / 0.95%, A r2 1.716 s / 0.83%, B r1 0.273 s / 0.36%, B r2 0.175 s / 0.16%, C r1 0.184 s / 0.29%, C r2 0.248 s / 0.25%; the largest prompt tok/s CV is 0.95%.",
